  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Philippines Cyclone Rai/Odette 2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cyclone RAI/ODETTE has made landfall in the Philippines on the afternoon of Thursday 16th December, categorized Red alert (level 5) by GDACS. Governmental and Red Cross Assessment teams are currently deployed, and initial reports are expected 17.12.2021, with more information coming in the next 72h. It is estimated that 15.9 million people living in the affected areas, out of which 3.5 million vulnerable in the most affected areas.&#xA0;
&#xA0;
The IFRC have launched a 24 month appeal for 20 million CHF, covering 405,000 families or 81,000 people. This will start on the 16th December 2021, and end on the 31st December 2023</narrative>
  </description>
